---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import TopicPosts from '../components/TopicPosts.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { posts, matchesCategory } from '../lib/blog';
const entries = (await posts()).filter(post => ['Writing', 'Creative Writing', 'Fanfiction'].some(category => matchesCategory(post, category)));
---
<PageLayout title="Stories beyond the screen" description="Fanfiction, half-whispered ideas, and the imagined worlds growing in my notebook." eyebrow="THE WRITING DESK"><section class="panel writing-intro prose"><Icon name="pen" size={30} /><h2>What if the story went another way?</h2><p>Sometimes a character stays with me long after a story ends. I start wondering about another choice, a quieter moment, a different beginning. This is where those thoughts find a page.</p><div class="project-card"><span class="eyebrow">IN MY NOTEBOOK · FANFICTION IN PROGRESS</span><h3>Another path for Louise</h3><p>An alternative story inspired by Louise from <cite>Zero no Tsukaima / The Familiar of Zero</cite>. I'm exploring how a different choice could lead her towards a new understanding of herself and the people around her.</p><p class="project-note">A personal, unofficial work of transformative fanfiction. The original characters and world belong to their respective rights holders. No original dialogue or source text is reproduced here.</p></div><h3>Little seeds of stories</h3><p>A letter that arrives from an impossible place. A familiar world seen through someone else's eyes. A small act of kindness that changes the ending. These are the kinds of ideas I like to collect.</p></section><div class="section-heading"><h2>From the writing notebook</h2></div><TopicPosts entries={entries} headingLevel="h3" /></PageLayout>
